merge(java.io.ObjectInputFilter,java.io..description:
Returns a filter that merges the status of a filter and another filter.
 If another filter is null, the filter is returned.
 Otherwise, a filter is returned to merge the pair of non-null filters.

 The filter returned implements the checkInput(FilterInfo) method
 as follows:

Invoke filter on the FilterInfo to get its status;
     Return REJECTED if the status is REJECTED;
     Invoke anotherFilter to get the otherStatus;
     Return REJECTED if the otherStatus is REJECTED;
     Return ALLOWED, if either status or otherStatus
          is ALLOWED, 
Otherwise, return UNDECIDED

rejectUndecidedClass(java.io.ObjectInput.notes:
Implementation Requirements:
The filter returned implements the checkInput(FilterInfo) method
 as follows:

Invoke the filter on the FilterInfo to get its status;
     Return the status if the status is REJECTED or ALLOWED;
     Return UNDECIDED if the filterInfo.getSerialClass() serialClass
          is null;
     Return REJECTED if the class is not an array;
     Determine the base component type if the serialClass is
          an array;
     Return UNDECIDED if the base component type is
          a primitive class;
     Invoke the filter on the base component type to get its
          component status;
Return ALLOWED if the component status is ALLOWED;
     Otherwise, return REJECTED.

Parameters:
filter - a filter
Returns:
an ObjectInputFilter that maps an ObjectInputFilter.Status.UNDECIDED
      status to ObjectInputFilter.Status.REJECTED for classes, otherwise returns the
      filter status
Since:
17

